WEBVTT

00:00:01.236 --> 00:00:06.096
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:07.136 --> 00:00:12.596
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:24.116 --> 00:00:29.386
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:34.756
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.996 --> 00:00:41.266
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.806 --> 00:00:47.006
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:50.936
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:55.886
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.686 --> 00:01:01.086
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.826 --> 00:01:08.786
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.866 --> 00:01:14.766
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.836 --> 00:01:21.406
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:27.616
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:57.146 --> 00:01:59.046
Do you have
good news for me?

00:02:01.656 --> 00:02:02.616
Come on now...

00:02:02.686 --> 00:02:05.516
Why'd you call me if
you have nothing to say?

00:02:05.926 --> 00:02:08.756
You think I have time to
just hang out with you?

00:02:10.726 --> 00:02:11.716
You can have it back.

00:02:14.696 --> 00:02:15.826
Why?

00:02:16.196 --> 00:02:16.826
I...

00:02:17.096 --> 00:02:17.496
Huh?

00:02:18.406 --> 00:02:20.526
...don't want to have anything
to do with you anymore.

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:21.866
Wha...?!

00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:23.036
See ya.

00:02:23.736 --> 00:02:25.436
You'll regret it later.

00:02:25.746 --> 00:02:26.676
No, I won't.

00:02:26.806 --> 00:02:27.676
We'll see.

00:02:27.876 --> 00:02:30.536
You better take care of that.

00:02:34.246 --> 00:02:35.646
What do I do now?

00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:44.486
This is a problem.

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:46.826
There's nothing we
can do about the past.

00:02:46.896 --> 00:02:47.726
Sakisaka!

00:02:47.936 --> 00:02:48.626
What?

00:02:48.696 --> 00:02:51.326
You're the problem since
you're the one that attacked.

00:02:51.806 --> 00:02:53.066
I told you not to.

00:02:53.436 --> 00:02:55.196
Now what?

00:02:55.506 --> 00:02:57.406
What're we going to do now?

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.306
We go out in the field
and we get attacked.

00:03:00.706 --> 00:03:03.406
We go to town,
thinking it's safe...

00:03:03.476 --> 00:03:05.316
...and we end up being followed.

00:03:09.586 --> 00:03:12.116
But even if something
happens we'll be okay!

00:03:12.886 --> 00:03:13.786
Why?

00:03:14.356 --> 00:03:17.916
I just need to stick with
you and everyone else!

00:03:22.566 --> 00:03:25.156
Even so, you need
to be very careful.

00:03:25.266 --> 00:03:25.636
Yup!

00:03:26.066 --> 00:03:29.196
And Haseo will come right
away as soon as I email him!

00:03:29.276 --> 00:03:29.636
What?

00:03:30.136 --> 00:03:31.436
Well, you did.

00:03:31.646 --> 00:03:32.536
That was...

00:03:32.606 --> 00:03:34.046
You don't have to be embarrassed!

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:38.116
Well, it didn't seem like
you came just to rescue me...

00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:40.646
...but I was happy that you came.

00:03:43.616 --> 00:03:46.746
But remember to RCDC.
Check everything twice.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.816
What? RCDC?

00:03:49.026 --> 00:03:51.186
Report. Communicate. Discuss.

00:03:51.266 --> 00:03:51.986
Check.

00:03:52.396 --> 00:03:55.486
In any case, if anything happens,
be sure to communicate.

00:03:55.736 --> 00:03:56.326
Okay?

00:03:56.396 --> 00:03:57.226
I guess.

00:03:57.296 --> 00:03:58.096
Yup!

00:03:58.466 --> 00:03:59.936
Haseo, do you understand?

00:04:00.266 --> 00:04:02.826
Yeah. RCDC.

00:04:03.806 --> 00:04:05.566
Always check twice.

00:04:06.676 --> 00:04:09.006
Hey, don't you think there are
a lot of TaN members around?

00:04:09.176 --> 00:04:09.906
Yeah.

00:04:10.046 --> 00:04:11.346
Maybe something happened.

00:04:12.216 --> 00:04:13.546
Did something happen?

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.176
Huh?

00:04:14.856 --> 00:04:15.506
Look.

00:04:17.116 --> 00:04:22.256
Maybe the rumor that TaN is
misleading the brigade is true.

00:04:22.726 --> 00:04:25.886
It seems it has something to do
with the Key of the Twilight.

00:04:26.396 --> 00:04:28.886
I wonder if they found
a clue or something.

00:04:29.096 --> 00:04:30.186
Does that bother you?

00:04:31.966 --> 00:04:33.166
It's not that.

00:04:34.576 --> 00:04:36.536
Since Haseo showed up...

00:04:36.606 --> 00:04:38.406
...something's weird
about the brigade.

00:04:39.046 --> 00:04:42.446
Do you really think
it's because of Haseo?

00:04:42.546 --> 00:04:43.446
No.

00:04:44.176 --> 00:04:46.616
A guild that was created
by an eccentric man.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:50.046
Perhaps there's been something
strange about it from the start.

00:04:52.556 --> 00:04:55.646
Isn't that why you left?

00:04:56.096 --> 00:04:58.926
There's nothing I can say to that.

00:05:06.766 --> 00:05:08.366
That's all you've got?

00:05:10.406 --> 00:05:11.776
It's me. It's me.

00:05:11.976 --> 00:05:13.036
Oh.

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.706
You sure put on a big show again.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.216
They weren't even good
enough for practice.

00:05:18.486 --> 00:05:20.206
So, what do you want?

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.646
I have information
on the problem item.

00:05:22.716 --> 00:05:23.946
What is it?

00:05:24.016 --> 00:05:24.916
Oh, nothing.

00:05:24.986 --> 00:05:28.946
But I think this item has something
to do with the "Key of the Twilight".

00:05:29.526 --> 00:05:31.256
But it was only a rumor.

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:34.326
Defeat Ovan.

00:05:36.236 --> 00:05:38.596
I know who has it.

00:05:39.306 --> 00:05:40.896
I bet you'd like to know.

00:05:42.636 --> 00:05:44.036
How much?

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.466
How about this much?

00:05:45.576 --> 00:05:46.596
50,000 huh?

00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:49.976
If it's useless, you'll be sorry!

00:05:51.916 --> 00:05:54.006
Hey, on my way here...

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:57.216
...I heard of a PK who's
targeting the Brigade.

00:05:57.286 --> 00:05:58.546
I heard that, too.

00:05:58.656 --> 00:06:00.486
I think it was someone
from our guild.

00:06:00.756 --> 00:06:01.846
Seriously?

00:06:02.326 --> 00:06:04.986
After we got a hold of
our own exclusive area?

00:06:05.066 --> 00:06:06.046
That's a joke!

00:06:06.126 --> 00:06:08.996
Why doesn't Mr. Tawaraya just
stop the rumors right away?

00:06:09.166 --> 00:06:11.066
Yeah, really. I mean...

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:13.066
...how can they be called
the "Twilight Brigade"?

00:06:13.136 --> 00:06:15.626
The Key of the Twilight
doesn't even exist.

00:06:16.506 --> 00:06:17.636
No kidding.

00:06:18.776 --> 00:06:19.906
What's their problem?

00:06:22.176 --> 00:06:25.546
Fine. But I don't really
like working so overtly.

00:06:26.016 --> 00:06:28.446
It's not like you to be concerned.

00:06:29.086 --> 00:06:29.916
So?

00:06:31.756 --> 00:06:35.486
I set out the bait
for the Brigade...

00:06:35.996 --> 00:06:37.896
...but nobody wants to bite.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:40.756
I'll put the pressure on.

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:42.356
Really heavy.

00:06:42.896 --> 00:06:45.426
Leave the bargaining
and calculating up to me.

00:06:46.236 --> 00:06:49.226
I'm not worried about you.

00:06:49.736 --> 00:06:51.606
Either way, it really
doesn't matter.

00:06:51.906 --> 00:06:54.466
As long as no one knows
you're part of TaN...

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:56.236
...we'll be fine.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:57.906
And if they knew?

00:06:57.976 --> 00:06:58.636
What?

00:06:59.046 --> 00:06:59.946
Do they know?

00:07:00.116 --> 00:07:03.946
Even if they know who Ender is,
it won't be a problem.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:04.586
Hm?

00:07:05.056 --> 00:07:08.686
TaN isn't a guild that can
be shaken so easily, right?

00:07:09.456 --> 00:07:10.516
Well, I suppose.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.286
We'll shake up the brigade first.

00:07:13.996 --> 00:07:18.366
By showing them the way to
the Key of the Twilight.

00:07:28.516 --> 00:07:29.606
Hey, hey!

00:07:29.876 --> 00:07:30.746
What?

00:07:30.946 --> 00:07:34.576
Isn't Ovan going to do
anything about this situation?

00:07:34.646 --> 00:07:37.316
No, he won't do anything.

00:07:38.456 --> 00:07:41.826
It seems to me that Shino's
more like the guild master.

00:07:45.866 --> 00:07:48.696
Huh? Where did Haseo go?

00:07:50.066 --> 00:07:53.096
Probably to check the
information from the other day.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:56.406
He could've taken us along.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.136
It's dangerous to go alone.

00:07:58.546 --> 00:08:01.836
He doesn't understand "RCDC".

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:07.106
Haseo doesn't discuss anything.

00:08:21.596 --> 00:08:22.626
What are you doing?

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.796
I've been watching you.

00:08:26.206 --> 00:08:27.296
Why are you standing there?

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:28.566
No reason.

00:08:29.276 --> 00:08:31.036
You're in the way.
So do you mind moving?

00:08:32.406 --> 00:08:33.336
Um, look...

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:33.936
What?

00:08:34.406 --> 00:08:35.006
Well...

00:08:35.376 --> 00:08:36.136
Um...

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:38.806
Nothing.

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:42.806
If you get stuck...

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:45.256
...start looking in
the places you can go.

00:08:45.526 --> 00:08:45.986
Huh?

00:08:46.756 --> 00:08:48.226
That's what I did.

00:08:50.126 --> 00:08:52.596
I'm giving advice to a newbie?

00:08:52.666 --> 00:08:54.526
What am I doing?

00:09:09.676 --> 00:09:12.706
Did you predict this situation?

00:09:12.816 --> 00:09:14.906
What do you mean by
"this situation"?

00:09:15.116 --> 00:09:16.276
The pressure from TaN.

00:09:18.386 --> 00:09:21.326
Is this what you were hoping for?

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:26.396
Since you're acquainted
with Naobi from TaN...

00:09:26.466 --> 00:09:27.866
...can't you do anything?

00:09:28.236 --> 00:09:30.896
It's already gone too far.

00:09:32.236 --> 00:09:34.036
I can take it...

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:37.436
...but I feel bad for Haseo
and Tabby who just started.

00:09:37.976 --> 00:09:41.606
They're just facing what was
already bound to happen.

00:09:42.116 --> 00:09:43.276
What do you mean?

00:09:43.876 --> 00:09:47.546
It just means we're
getting closer to the core.

00:09:55.096 --> 00:09:57.186
I'll be back at work for some time.

00:09:57.356 --> 00:10:01.126
Are you in trouble for being
absent from work for so long?

00:10:02.136 --> 00:10:04.256
It's hard to explain.

00:10:04.696 --> 00:10:05.666
I know.

00:10:06.366 --> 00:10:09.566
I like to think that I
understand your work.

00:10:10.336 --> 00:10:12.366
While I'm away...

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:16.106
We can proceed as usual, right?

00:10:16.776 --> 00:10:17.806
I'll leave it to you.

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:20.346
If we know the whereabouts of
the remaining Virus Cores...

00:10:20.446 --> 00:10:21.476
Where do we look?

00:10:21.686 --> 00:10:23.116
The Lost Grounds.

00:10:24.986 --> 00:10:26.246
The rest doesn't matter.

00:10:26.526 --> 00:10:27.746
Just the four of us?

00:10:27.986 --> 00:10:28.756
Three.

00:10:29.696 --> 00:10:30.416
What about me?

00:10:30.926 --> 00:10:32.656
Wait for my communication.

00:10:48.076 --> 00:10:50.376
Hey, got a second?

00:10:51.916 --> 00:10:52.676
What is it?

00:10:52.816 --> 00:10:56.586
I came to steal an item that
you've been carefully protecting.

00:10:56.956 --> 00:10:59.616
Came to steal it? That's crude.

00:10:59.926 --> 00:11:02.416
If I asked you, would
you give it to me?

00:11:02.496 --> 00:11:04.286
What are you talking about?

00:11:04.356 --> 00:11:08.156
Old man, don't hide it from
me. I already have proof.

00:11:08.696 --> 00:11:10.026
All right...

00:11:10.166 --> 00:11:12.036
Follow me.

00:11:21.506 --> 00:11:23.446
If that's all you got...

00:11:23.516 --> 00:11:26.446
...how can you "defeat Ovan"?

00:11:28.886 --> 00:11:31.856
The truth is, I don't
have it anymore.

00:11:31.926 --> 00:11:32.786
Wh-What?

00:11:32.956 --> 00:11:36.586
I wanted to teach you
a lesson in manners.

00:11:36.796 --> 00:11:38.586
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:11:38.666 --> 00:11:41.026
I know which PC has it though.

00:11:41.096 --> 00:11:43.996
You're not going to tell
me the truth, are you?

00:11:44.836 --> 00:11:46.196
I don't mind.

00:11:46.336 --> 00:11:50.036
But of the items that have been
confirmed, the Brigade has half.

00:11:51.136 --> 00:11:53.906
Is there more than
one Virus Core?

00:11:54.246 --> 00:11:55.306
I think so.

00:11:55.376 --> 00:11:57.176
TaN has one, too.

00:11:57.246 --> 00:11:58.976
Where's the one that you had?

00:11:59.046 --> 00:12:00.536
I gave it to Shino.

00:12:00.946 --> 00:12:03.386
I'm sure the Brigade
is taking care of it.

00:12:03.616 --> 00:12:05.016
Aren't there any more?

00:12:05.356 --> 00:12:08.226
I don't have that
kind of information.

00:12:08.526 --> 00:12:12.056
But rumor has it there are as
many as there are Lost Grounds.

00:12:12.466 --> 00:12:14.056
Lost Grounds?

00:12:14.526 --> 00:12:15.426
Five.

00:12:15.536 --> 00:12:18.626
No, another one
was found, so six.

00:12:19.336 --> 00:12:22.366
Okay, if you get any
information, tell me!

00:12:23.836 --> 00:12:26.606
Is that how you ask
someone for something?

00:12:26.806 --> 00:12:29.936
I hate being humble.

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:32.406
I can see that!

00:13:00.376 --> 00:13:02.506
So, an item isn't in the specs...

00:13:04.016 --> 00:13:04.846
This is it, huh?

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:52.026
Meow!

00:13:55.866 --> 00:13:56.556
Hey...

00:13:56.696 --> 00:13:57.496
Huh?

00:13:57.566 --> 00:13:59.766
What do you think about
what happened the other day?

00:14:00.406 --> 00:14:03.526
Are you talking about that
meteor shower-like incident?

00:14:03.606 --> 00:14:04.336
Yeah.

00:14:04.406 --> 00:14:07.136
If that was the monster
that drops Virus Cores...

00:14:07.206 --> 00:14:09.196
...then we just let it get away.

00:14:09.276 --> 00:14:11.336
I don't think so.

00:14:11.676 --> 00:14:14.516
So far, I've never
heard of a monster...

00:14:14.586 --> 00:14:17.106
...that can disintegrate weapons.

00:14:17.286 --> 00:14:21.246
Isn't that why it might be related
to an item that's not in the specs?

00:14:21.426 --> 00:14:22.756
No, of course not.

00:14:22.826 --> 00:14:25.346
It's more like, let's see...

00:14:25.626 --> 00:14:26.456
More like?

00:14:26.596 --> 00:14:29.426
Oh, come on! You know.

00:14:29.936 --> 00:14:31.996
Kind of ominous or...

00:14:32.206 --> 00:14:32.996
I don't get it.

00:14:33.066 --> 00:14:34.866
Oh, I don't know.

00:14:45.786 --> 00:14:47.336
Did something happen?

00:14:49.016 --> 00:14:52.116
If nothing happened,
you wouldn't be here.

00:14:52.886 --> 00:14:53.686
I guess.

00:14:53.756 --> 00:14:54.886
So tell me.

00:14:55.556 --> 00:14:58.546
Does this game
have a lot of bugs?

00:14:59.366 --> 00:15:00.696
So something did happen.

00:15:01.196 --> 00:15:03.996
Just now all of a sudden
there was this disturbance.

00:15:04.366 --> 00:15:05.496
It happened before, too.

00:15:07.166 --> 00:15:08.656
Maybe it's nothing
to be worried about.

00:15:08.736 --> 00:15:11.866
Well, there have been
rumors like that.

00:15:12.376 --> 00:15:16.936
Nevertheless, they are rumors.

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:18.046
I see.

00:15:18.446 --> 00:15:20.536
Besides that, how
have you been lately?

00:15:20.916 --> 00:15:22.046
What do you mean?

00:15:22.256 --> 00:15:24.186
There are more threads
about the Brigade...

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:27.226
...than there are
mysterious rumors.

00:15:30.526 --> 00:15:34.986
I guess an eccentric man is
bound to attract attention.

00:15:36.736 --> 00:15:38.466
Did someone contact you?

00:15:39.466 --> 00:15:39.956
Um...

00:15:40.036 --> 00:15:40.766
Yeah?

00:15:41.136 --> 00:15:42.866
Do you think...

00:15:42.936 --> 00:15:44.376
No, never mind.

00:15:44.836 --> 00:15:45.396
Hey...

00:15:46.476 --> 00:15:50.536
Whenever I'm here, I'm
happy to give advice.

00:15:52.246 --> 00:15:54.216
I'm leaving for now.

00:15:58.286 --> 00:16:00.226
Haseo, you're late.

00:16:00.286 --> 00:16:00.986
Yeah.

00:16:01.226 --> 00:16:02.656
Everyone's here now.

00:16:04.126 --> 00:16:06.886
You're going to begin searching
for the Virus Cores again.

00:16:07.266 --> 00:16:09.236
You'll concentrate
on the Lost Grounds.

00:16:09.296 --> 00:16:09.996
What?!

00:16:11.236 --> 00:16:12.926
Uh, nothing.

00:16:13.836 --> 00:16:14.966
Hey, Shino...

00:16:15.166 --> 00:16:16.866
Why the Lost Grounds?

00:16:17.606 --> 00:16:22.976
All the Virus Cores found so
far appeared in a Lost Ground.

00:16:24.176 --> 00:16:26.446
Even the one you have?

00:16:26.886 --> 00:16:27.676
Yes.

00:16:27.846 --> 00:16:31.446
But, at a time like this, do
you really think it's wise?

00:16:31.786 --> 00:16:34.016
We don't know how
long this will last.

00:16:34.286 --> 00:16:36.556
Are you planning on
waiting 'til TaN gives up?

00:16:36.626 --> 00:16:37.956
I guess not.

00:16:38.296 --> 00:16:40.286
The purpose of the
Twilight Brigade is to...

00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:44.356
...find the Key of the Twilight
that may or may not exist.

00:16:44.496 --> 00:16:44.936
Right.

00:16:45.136 --> 00:16:45.896
So...

00:16:45.966 --> 00:16:46.836
What do we do?

00:16:47.206 --> 00:16:50.036
Sakisaka, Tabby and Haseo...

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:51.236
I'll leave it up to you.

00:16:51.306 --> 00:16:52.036
What about you?

00:16:53.106 --> 00:16:55.596
We can't have more than
three in the party.

00:16:55.776 --> 00:16:58.336
I'll be waiting for
Ovan's communication.

00:16:58.576 --> 00:17:00.016
Well, shall we go?

00:17:00.246 --> 00:17:00.806
Sure...

00:17:14.426 --> 00:17:16.986
How should we look for them?

00:17:17.096 --> 00:17:19.566
It's an item that isn't in the specs.

00:17:20.506 --> 00:17:23.596
I wonder if Shino is on a
date with her boyfriend.

00:17:24.006 --> 00:17:24.696
A date?

00:17:25.106 --> 00:17:26.576
Of course not.

00:17:26.706 --> 00:17:28.366
She denied it last time.

00:17:28.446 --> 00:17:30.276
Stop jumping to so
many conclusions.

00:17:30.846 --> 00:17:31.746
Okay.

00:17:33.486 --> 00:17:34.246
Did you believe me?

00:17:34.316 --> 00:17:35.216
Not really.

00:17:36.216 --> 00:17:37.016
It doesn't matter, anyway.

00:17:41.786 --> 00:17:43.486
Are you jealous?

00:17:43.556 --> 00:17:44.856
Why would I be?

00:17:44.926 --> 00:17:47.526
Well, you always
avoid looking at her.

00:17:50.266 --> 00:17:52.356
A man can't face
the woman he adores.

00:17:54.266 --> 00:17:56.796
There's no treasure
box or monsters!

00:17:57.436 --> 00:18:00.466
How are we supposed
to find it here?!

00:18:00.546 --> 00:18:01.806
They could be on the ground.

00:18:02.276 --> 00:18:03.206
You know what?

00:18:03.976 --> 00:18:06.446
It's not going to be
that easy to find them!

00:18:17.056 --> 00:18:18.886
What is this?

00:18:19.026 --> 00:18:20.586
Some kind of pattern?

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:24.116
No, there are no such
patterns in this game.

00:18:29.806 --> 00:18:31.106
I wonder what it is?

00:18:32.376 --> 00:18:33.636
I see.

00:18:34.376 --> 00:18:36.406
That's why, Tawaraya...

00:18:36.476 --> 00:18:41.476
...you need to find the Key of
the Twilight before Ovan does.

00:18:41.846 --> 00:18:43.046
Leave it to me.

00:18:44.916 --> 00:18:45.646
Report.

00:18:46.056 --> 00:18:48.986
The brigade guys
look pretty calm...

00:18:49.556 --> 00:18:51.756
...but under the surface
they're anxious.

00:18:51.826 --> 00:18:53.916
I'm certain they're in a hurry.

00:18:53.996 --> 00:18:57.366
Haseo is most likely checking
out the information I gave him.

00:18:57.636 --> 00:18:58.996
I'm sure he'll bite.

00:18:59.066 --> 00:19:02.006
Tawaraya, would you leave us?

00:19:02.236 --> 00:19:02.896
Am I in the way?

00:19:03.436 --> 00:19:06.836
Sometimes it's better if
you don't know everything.

00:19:06.906 --> 00:19:07.706
I see.

00:19:12.486 --> 00:19:14.776
We'll stay here a little longer.

00:19:15.286 --> 00:19:16.476
Are we getting rid of him?

00:19:16.556 --> 00:19:18.246
Are the preparations going well?

00:19:18.316 --> 00:19:18.846
Yes.

00:19:19.286 --> 00:19:21.846
But is Ovan really going to come?

00:19:23.826 --> 00:19:27.386
He will, for the Key of the Twilight.

00:19:28.966 --> 00:19:31.056
That's what this huge setup is for.

00:19:31.136 --> 00:19:33.656
We can only catch one.

00:19:33.736 --> 00:19:35.096
That's not a problem.

00:19:35.236 --> 00:19:36.796
When everything's done,
what about Tawaraya?

00:19:36.876 --> 00:19:38.136
Just leave him for now.

00:19:38.506 --> 00:19:39.436
Understood.

00:19:39.846 --> 00:19:41.776
I'll return to my surveillance.

00:19:52.956 --> 00:19:56.156
This area's big, so they
might be around here.

00:20:19.086 --> 00:20:19.976
What's the matter?

00:20:20.386 --> 00:20:20.816
Huh?

00:20:21.686 --> 00:20:23.476
This is a weird place, huh?

00:20:23.556 --> 00:20:25.956
I have no idea why it's here.

00:20:26.526 --> 00:20:27.816
Don't you think?

00:20:28.686 --> 00:20:29.156
Yeah.

00:20:29.956 --> 00:20:31.086
Anything wrong?

00:20:31.756 --> 00:20:32.316
Huh?

00:20:33.596 --> 00:20:35.526
You're hiding
something, aren't you?

00:20:35.696 --> 00:20:36.256
Huh?

00:20:37.596 --> 00:20:39.936
Just don't betray us.

00:20:42.876 --> 00:20:44.736
Over here! Over here!

00:20:48.376 --> 00:20:49.576
What is this?

00:20:59.956 --> 00:21:01.586
This isn't a coincidence.

00:21:01.986 --> 00:21:02.816
This is...

00:21:02.896 --> 00:21:04.446
It's not that simple.

00:21:04.756 --> 00:21:06.486
There's more Lost Grounds.

00:21:06.566 --> 00:21:08.086
I know, but...

00:21:09.266 --> 00:21:10.096
You know what?

00:21:10.966 --> 00:21:12.596
Let's go to the next place.

00:21:12.666 --> 00:21:15.196
We need to get serious about
finding the Virus Cores.

00:21:16.436 --> 00:21:17.736
Quit wasting time!

00:21:17.836 --> 00:21:18.666
Uh, okay!

00:21:37.926 --> 00:21:38.256
Hey!

00:22:30.246 --> 00:22:33.836
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.916 --> 00:22:37.356
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:37.616 --> 00:22:41.346
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:41.426 --> 00:22:45.446
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:49.036 --> 00:22:52.556
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:52.636 --> 00:22:56.266
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:56.336 --> 00:23:03.576
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:03.646 --> 00:23:07.306
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:11.076
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:11.156 --> 00:23:18.086
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:18.256 --> 00:23:21.996
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:22.066 --> 00:23:25.086
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:25.166 --> 00:23:32.626
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.876 --> 00:23:36.076
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:36.146 --> 00:23:40.176
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:40.286 --> 00:23:43.876
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.956 --> 00:23:47.586
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:47.656 --> 00:23:51.386
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:51.456 --> 00:23:55.156
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:56.366 --> 00:23:59.336
Next Episode...
